---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  lang="en"
  title="Aevra Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for Aevra — how we collect, use, and protect your personal information."
>
  <div class="legal-page">
    <header class="legal-header">
      <h1 style="margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;">Aevra Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Effective Date: February 12, 2026</p>
      <p>Last Updated: February 12, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Account data, such as Apple sign-in identifier, email, and profile name if provided.</li>
        <li>Content data, such as text you submit and interaction records (for example, Glimmer and Echo).</li>
        <li>Device and log data, such as device model, OS version, crash logs, IP address, and timestamps.</li>
        <li>Transaction status for subscriptions and in-app purchases processed by Apple.</li>
        <li>Support communications you send to us.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>2. How We Use Information</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide, secure, maintain, and improve the Service.</li>
        <li>Prevent abuse, fraud, and policy violations.</li>
        <li>Handle account, purchase, and support requests.</li>
        <li>Comply with legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>3. Sharing of Information</h2>
      <p>We do not sell your personal information.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Service providers that process data on our behalf (for hosting, storage, analytics, support).</li>
        <li>Legal and regulatory disclosures when required by law or valid legal process.</li>
        <li>Business transfer scenarios, subject to confidentiality protections.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain personal information only as long as needed for the purposes described in this policy, unless a
        longer period is required by law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>5. Your Rights</h2>
      <p>
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, and receive a copy of your personal
        information, and to object to or limit certain processing.
      </p>
      <p>
        For California residents, rights may include those under CCPA/CPRA, including non-discrimination for exercising
        privacy rights.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>6. Children’s Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is not directed to children under 13. If we learn we collected personal information from a child
        under 13 without required consent, we will delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>7. Tracking and ATT</h2>
      <p>
        We do not perform cross-app or cross-site tracking without permission. If tracking is introduced, we will first
        request consent through Apple’s App Tracking Transparency prompt where required.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>8. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards, including encryption in transit and access controls.
        No system can be guaranteed 100% secure.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>9. Policy Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy. If changes are material, we will provide notice through the app, website, or other
        reasonable means.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>10. Contact</h2>
      <p>Email: <a href="mailto:aevra@echoversa.com">aevra@echoversa.com</a></p>
    </section>

    <footer class="legal-footer">
      <a href="/">Back Home</a>
      <span>·</span>
      <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a>
      <span>·</span>
      <a href="/zh/privacy">中文</a>
    </footer>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
